please define 'best' Sparc - this is still way too vague. I regularly
use a range of machines including Sparc 5/110, Ultra1/140, Ultra1/170
(all running Solaris) and PPro180 running Linux 2.0.30. My
PC will blow any of the Sparc's out of the water on graphics -
the Sparcs have the cheapest Sun color graphics, and is about 2-3
times faster than the Sparc 5 on general stuff. However even
slightly numerically intensive programs (generally manipulating
gridded data files) or anything that calls for memory bandwidth
are 2-3 times faster on the Ultras than my PC.

The fastest desktop Ultras these days are running at 300MHz with 2-4Mb
L2 cache from what I understand, and benchmark about twice as fast
as the Ultra1's we use right now (ie 5-6 times faster than the PPro
if the SPEC benchmarks are at all representative). If you dont use a
high-end graphics card in them tho' the perceived performance for
graphical stuff still probably sucks, the moral being that you choose
your platform for what you want to run. something like web serving for
a smallish site doesnot require much copmuting power - our departmental
web server is a Sparc 2, state of the art ca. 1990!
also remember that the desktop
PC you apparently need to run word processing these days is as fast
as second generation Crays...

