In article <606djj$k0v@milo.mcs.anl.gov>,
Donald K.Sinclair  <dks@sgi9.hep.anl.gov> wrote:
>The vendor claimed that
>they had configured systems with swap partitions as large as 1 Gbyte which
>appeared to be usable. Does this mean that there is a larger limit for the
>size of swap partitions on Linux Alpha than Linux Intel, or is the vendor in
>error?

Both.  The limit is based on one page of "in-use" bits, thus the
max usable swap varies with the square of the page size.  Thus the
max usable swap parition on the Alpha is 4 times larger than on
Intel, i.e. 512MB.


