Reply-To: ewt@redhat.com
Newsgroups: comp.os.linux.alpha,comp.os.linux.x


On 25 Sep 1997 22:20:36 GMT, Timothy Ryan Cleary <tryanc@athena.mit.edu> wrote:
>Does anyone know why all these chipsets aren't part of the XF86_SVGA
>in XFree86 v3.3.1, or where I can get support for the 'generic'
>or 'Advance Logic' chipsets? 

Porting X servers to the Alpha can be quite a bit of work. They tend
to do a lot of 8-bit addressing to memory and I/O space, which is
horribly inefficient on the Alpha. Much of the code is also littered
with long/int/pointer confusion, which is time-consuming to fix. Due to
these concerns, the folks who keep X on the Alpha running aren't that
interested in trying to support old or unpopular chipsets.

Erik

