On Sun, 14 Sep 1997, Phillip G Ezolt <pe28+@andrew.cmu.edu> wrote:
>
>Ok,
>    Fine, Windows is not the ideal platform. (far far from it)  The
>ideal platform would not come to a crawl when the network is removed.
>In order to make linux that ideal platform, it should not be dependent
>on network connectivity to be moderately usable. 

You'll probably find, (I did) that RH4 wants to fire up into runlevel 3 by
default, which loads EVERYTHING. nfs, ypstuff, smb, news, etc. You'll most
probably find for most people, that stuff isn't really needed (yp?! Put
your hands up if you use yp on your Linux box!)

Either change your default runlevel to 2, but add the networking bits that
you need, or keep it at 3, and delete the bits you don't (most often, for
a home Linux box, ypstuff, news) Mainly ypstuff, especially if it can't
find a domain master.


