>Serial number of failed request: 49
>Current serial number in output stream: 50

That is a known problem, that I once solved. See the archive of the redhat-axp
mailing-list, that may be found on www.redhat.com ; there is a search
engine. You may find a rather long mail of mine, explaining the problem
and the solution I used (use my name as keyword, it should work rather well).

Basically, it is an incompatibility between the structs used to control
shared memory in the kernel and in the libs. You may either find an old
X11 server that handles shared memory the old way, or patch the kernel
to behave correctly. The axp-diff may help you with a 2.0.x kernel.
Recent 2.1.x kernels do not have the problem, but are development,
not-so-stable kernels.

	--Thomas Pornin



