[ ... Horrendous performance figures ... ]

> One of several things is wrong. It's not the memory system, as I observe
> flat performance up to the 256 MBytes
> of memory on the machine.
> 
> I think the compiler is the culprit. Any ideas?

This sort of code tends to benefit rather handsomely from the optimisation 
known as "strength reduction", basically changing all array index arithmetic 
by simple stride 4 (or 8 in case of DOUBLE PRECISION) steps through the 
arrays.

However, in g77 "strength reduction" is almost completely ineffective on the 
Alpha, because the optimisation pass doesn't know how to deal with subword 
integers (the default INTEGER in g77 is 32 bits wide, which is half of a 
64-bit register).

I'm working on a solution to this problem, but so far I've produced nothing 
more than a patch purely as a Gedankenexperiment (on a Motorola 68040 based 
NEXTSTATION ;-)

