I don't know much about the Alpha (besides that it's fast), but I can offer a
few commnets on Sparc hardware vs. PC hardware. Here at OSU, they have found
that a Pentium (not a Petium II) running FreeBSD could go toe-to-toe with the
best Sparc for a quarter of the money. Hence, the next generation of Web
server and file servers will be Pentiums.  

If you need top-notch floating point (for heavy number crunching, like
finite element codes), I'd look at the Alpha. The PC will be weak here. 
If you just want a basic UNIX workstation, I'd look at PC hardware. 
Your dollar will travel much farther.

>
>Also, does anyone have something brief to say about DEC Unix, vs Solaris,
>vs Linux?  We are used to Solaris.  Will Linux give us a similar nice
>graphical interface.

Performance-wise, on the same hardware, Linux will leave Solaris in the dust.  

If you like the Common Desktop Environment (CDE), I'd look at some of Caldera's
offerings. I think they offer a distribution of linux which includes Motif and
CDE. It will cost a bit more, but will give you a familiar interface.

They also have good support packages, should you need to go that route.

Sorry I don't have much to say about the alpha. 

Mike

