This kind of statement is misleading.  What you mean to say is your
informal impression of a pentium is that it is as fast as the "best"
SPARC.  I would take a look at the SPEC website
http://open.specbench.org/.  Comparing a 300 MHz Pentium II to a 300MHz
SPARC shows they are almost equal in interger performance, but the SPARC
is roughly 3 times faster at floating point.  Unless you have really
specialized code, SPEC numbers are probably the best available for
comparison.

