Hi -

In article <Pine.SGI.3.95q.970917150855.19017E-100000@zeus.bris.ac.uk>, A. Rodriguez-Gonzalez wrote:
>
>	Hi everybody:
>
>	Does anyone know where i could find some benchmarks of Alpha
>systems running Linux compared with ... say P200 or P166. I've been
>looking around but i couln't find the same test performed in both
>systems.

I've benchmarked one of our 500MHz Alphas running both Linux and NT, as well
as an iP5-150. I used the BYTEbench version 2 (10/95). The numbers I got
were:

500MHz Alpha (Linux): Integer 7.615, Floating Point 3.322
500MHz Alpha (NT)   :         6.950                 8.081
iP5-150 (Linux)     :         1.778                 1.346

I also found this report of a Pentium-II, 233MHz

iPII-233 (Linux)    :         3.527                 2.870

The P-II and the 500MHz Alpha were very similarly configured (e.g. 7200RPM
SCSI HDD, 64M memory, 4M Millenium video [which is not a factor in this
benchmark]).

Also note the artifact of the FP performance under Linux. This may be down
the the maths library or the benchmark performing some operation which is
distinctly un-optimal on Alpha. I suspect the former, as indicated by the NT
benchmark result.

Anybody more knowlegable about libm care to comment?

