Ian,

IG> I have an axp150 box currenlty running Windows NT 3.51.  I want to install
IG> Linux on the box.  I have lost my ECU (EISA Config Utility) disk for the
IG> machine.  Does anyone have any ideas where I can get one from ???

If you don't add, remove or move any EISA or ISA boards in your system,
you won't need it when installing Linux.

You must switch to the SRM console in order to install Linux and it can't
coexist with NT on the same disk, because the SRM wants a BSD disklabel rather
than a normally with Fdisk partitioned disk. You should first read all the
Jensen related stuff before attempting to install Linux. I can send you the
SRM-HOWTO but you should find it on the distribution CD as well. You should get
Aboot, there's no Milo for the Jensen.

In case you need one, a (rather old) ECU can be found at GATEKEEPER.DEC.COM (as
far as I remember.) If you don't find one, I'll send you the floppy or mail it
to you later.

Viele Gruesse, Christoph




