	cbbrowne@hex.net (Christopher Browne) writes:
> c) Is your processing actually CPU dependent?

You can find this out if you get a program like "top" and run it while
performing a task you want speeded up. What you are looking for is the
user CPU usage hitting the ceiling. If the kernel CPU usage hits the
ceiling or is higher than the user CPU usage, then it's highly likely
that you're hitting I/O bounds, not CPU bounds. For the vast majority
of tasks that I've seen, I/O bounds are the limit, which is why I'm
still running on a P133 and looking for faster disc access times.

