Ken Farwell (ken@pieceby.com) wrote:
: Ken here
: 	Not sure if this is a dead group or not but here goes, Installed 4.2
: from the CDRom at Milo did ls -l on /etc and found 
: drwxr-xr-x   2 root     root         1024 Sep  6  2017 cron.weekly

This is a common problem (we're not all living in the past :-)

The default setup for reading the time from the multia hardware clock is wrong
and if the arc time is set to the present, you'll get dates in 2017.

The fix is simple (ish):

Change /etc/sysconfig/clock to read

UTC=false
ARC=true

I also touched all files in the filesystem to set the dates correctly. If
you want to be really neat, there's sure to be a way to use find to find
all files created in the future and touch them but I just touched the lot.
