> CL(> : > It is a cute little machine and I want another computer to dedicate to
> CL(> : > Linux, but I don't want to spend $350 on a cute little computer that
> CL(> : > performs like a 486DX2-66.
> CL(> : the statement from a person from Digital on the CeBit
> CL(> : to similar questions to this machine was: "Forget it, the processor is
> CL(> : bad."
> 
> Well, I've read that the 21164 has built-in PCI capabilities, but other
> disadvantages in comparison with the 21064.
> 
 
the 21066 and 21068 are the chips which have built in PCI, they are also
known as LCA4 and LCA45 (low-cost-alpha),  they were the processors used
in the UDB (or multia) and a few entry level motherboards.  They
basically were (aside from the PCI and MMU) mem/io constrained (1/2 bus
width) EV4s (21064).  The advantages the 21068 had over the '066 was
higher clock rates (it was done in CMOS 5) and an enhanced floating
point unit.

the 21164 is the 2nd generation architectural implementation - EV5,56

just clearing things up
-scot

ps - oh on the performance side '066 ~ pentium66, '068 ~ pentium100



