> under the CPU.
>
> Unfortunately the tines are broken off and are still on the MB, but

You're fucked.  That's a 3.5 mA dual (male/female) external oryctolagi
cage, which handles split 16/32 bit multiply operations for the FPU.  
The little tines supply oxygen, and after you busted them off the
little beasts undoubtably asphyxiated right away.

Actually, the fact that these have spread all over the bottom of your
MB means you should probably replace it (the MB) anyway.  After you 
get too many of them growing down there you start seeing signal 11's
when recompiling the kernel and signal 7's when running Netscape.

You could try sending "kill TRAP -noskin" to init or deleting
all the files in /dev and then rebooting from an 8-track tape, but 
I've never heard of this working for long.

Good luck.

john



