They only seem stupid once you already know the answer, but we all started
as newbies once :)

> 
> 1: I have a CD written in Vfat (sounds odd, but dont ask k?) I currently 
> do not have Vfat support installed, how do I do it.. I know I have to 
> edit a file in /proc but I duno which one and how

With redhat, vfat should be there as a module.  What you're thinking of
with /proc is /proc/filesystems.  You don't edit anything in here, but
doing 'cat /proc/filesystems' will show you what filesystem drivers are
present at the moment.  Mounting the cdrom with something like
mount -t vfat /dev/scd0 /cdrom
should cause kerneld to load the vfat module, and mount the cdrom.

> 
> 2: is there a version of ARJ for linux, and where do I get it..
> 
> 3: is there a version of pkunzip for linux, and where do I get it..

You can find tools for both of these at
ftp://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/utils/compress 

