Michael Callahan  <callahan@[NOSPAM]xmission.com> wrote:
>It's about time for me to get a new computer, and I've been looking
>at the Alpha as a good alternative to the Intel for a cheap powerful
>Linux Workstation.  However, I'm having trouble finding information
>about Alpha hardware availability.

The LX motherboards aren't exactly the "low cost" motherboards--these
motherboards support the 21164A Alpha not the 21164PC.

www.dcginc.com and www.aspsys.com both have web pages describing
their PC164LX offerings.

The 21164PC and its motherboard, the PC164SX, won't be available until
October at the last report I've heard.

The LX motherboard's primary distinguishing feature is their support
of SDRAM.

It is likely you won't be able to get an LX motherboard directly from
DEC--I'd go directly to DCG or to Aspen or to one of the other
resellers right off.

If you REALLY want to buy from DEC, you could get one of the
Personal Workstations:  these support SDRAM as well, but I think they're
different from the PC164LX motherboards...

PeterM



