Actually, I've read the SPECmarks estimates that DEC has on their
websites for these boards:


                  Speed       SPECint95      SPECfp95      BYTE

                  533 MHz     14.3           17.0          N/A
                  466 MHz     12.5           15.0          N/A
                  400 MHz     10.7           13.0          N/A

This is from:
http://www.digital.com/semiconductor/alpha/alphapc64.htm

The PC164LX gets: (I think)
		  500MHz      15.7	     19.5

The "hit" is 9% for Int and 13% for Fp, which is NOT that severe for
~1/2 the price....

The lack of the 2nd-level 96k onchip cache is made up for, I think,
by the fact that the memory latency is reduced and the 1st level icache
is increased in size.  Also, the 2nd level offchip cache is faster
than was available when the 96k onchip cache of the 21164A was designed.

PeterM




